      "writtenOn": "2021-01-22T16:40:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This can be only really tested when TARGET_BUILD_APPS is nonempty, as it is the only case when boot images are built but nothing is dexpreopted (if someting is dexpreopted, it will provide the dependency). There are a few ways to test this:\n\n1. Build the ART module (it is possible to shorten the build time by commenting out all other modules in build_mainline_modules.sh):\n\n $ DIST_DIR\u003d$PWD/dist \\\n    TARGET_BUILD_VARIANT\u003duserdebug \\\n    vendor/google/build/build_mainline_modules.sh\n\n2. Forrest build for git_master, mainline_modules-userdebug.\n\nI expect that if something is wrong and the dex2oat dependency is not found, the the build will crash in dex2oatPathFromDep. The code is obvious, but can you do either of the two tests just in case?",
